<section class="page-hero bot-hero">
  <div class="hero-stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="shell bot-hero-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Discord companion</p>
      <h1>A cat in<br><em>your server.</em></h1>
      <p class="page-lede">
        Link a Discord account to Ei Void, ask for usage without unlocking the
        phone, and keep every reply private. The bot is a thin server-side
        client; the token never reaches this page.
      </p>
      <div class="page-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= site.discordInviteUrl %>" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Add Ei Void to Discord</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/dashboard">Open the dashboard <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <p class="small-note">
        Needs Manage Server to invite · application id
        <span class="mono"><%= site.discordApplicationId %></span>
      </p>
      <p class="bot-verification">
        <span class="chip chip-warn">Verification in preparation</span>
        The blue badge is a Discord review, not a switch in this site.
      </p>
    </div>
    <%- include('partials/discord-window') %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">The commands</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Three verbs, no noise.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Every reply is ephemeral and the bot is locked to its home server. It
        requests only the Guilds intent, never reads message content, and never
        sends DMs — closing your inbox does not hide /link or /usage.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="command-grid">
      <article class="command-card">
        <div class="command-name"><span class="slash" aria-hidden="true">/</span>link</div>
        <p>Creates a single-use, ten-minute URL where this Discord account confirms the link. It opens the website dashboard.</p>
        <p class="command-note">Only you can see the reply.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="command-card">
        <div class="command-name"><span class="slash" aria-hidden="true">/</span>usage</div>
        <p>Reads the latest snapshot for the linked account: plan, tokens used and the period limit.</p>
        <p class="command-note">If the app has not synced yet, it says so instead of inventing a zero.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="command-card">
        <div class="command-name"><span class="slash" aria-hidden="true">/</span>about</div>
        <p>One line about Ei Void, the repo and the account portal. The least dramatic command in the void.</p>
        <p class="command-note">No buttons, no modal, no telemetry.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="shell split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <p class="kicker">How linking works</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">A one-time door.</h2>
      <ol class="numbered-list">
        <li><span class="num">01</span><p>Run <code>/link</code> in any server where the bot is present.</p></li>
        <li><span class="num">02</span><p>Ei Void creates a 192-bit, single-use code and returns a private URL.</p></li>
        <li><span class="num">03</span><p>Open the URL. Confirm the Discord name. The website sets a signed, HttpOnly session.</p></li>
        <li><span class="num">04</span><p>Run <code>/usage</code> later. The bot asks the website for the latest snapshot.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/discord-bot">Read the bot guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="split-visual">
      <div class="callout">
        <span class="callout-mark" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
        <div>
          <p class="callout-title">The token is not a login secret.</p>
          <p>
            A Discord bot token belongs in the worker's environment. It cannot
            sign a user in, and it must never be placed in the Android app, a
            browser bundle, git or this page. The bot derives its application
            id from the token; the website only needs the public id for the
            invite button.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout callout-warn">
        <span class="callout-mark" aria-hidden="true">△</span>
        <div>
          <p class="callout-title">Usage sync is the missing bridge.</p>
          <p>
            The app keeps its usage ledger locally. The dashboard can issue a
            device key for the app to push counters; until an app build uses it,
            <code>/usage</code> reports “linked, not synced.” The API contract
            is public so the next build can close the loop.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head section-head-row">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Read the manual</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Operate the companion.</h2>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs">All docs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <%- include('partials/docs-grid', { items: botDocs }) %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="waitlist-section">
  <div class="shell waitlist waitlist-compact">
    <div class="waitlist-copy">
      <p class="kicker">The quiet community</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Bring the cat to your server.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        The invite works as soon as the Render worker is online. The worker
        needs the bot token; the website needs nothing from Discord but the
        public application id.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="waitlist-action">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= site.discordInviteUrl %>" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Add Ei Void to Discord</a>
      <p class="waitlist-note">Manage Server required · scopes: bot, applications.commands</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
